ker Execution Parameters

docker exec: Instructs Docker to run a command inside a container that is currently running in the background.

-i (--interactive): Keeps standard input (STDIN) open, allowing data transmission to the container.

-t (--tty): Allocates a pseudo-TTY (terminal emulator), formatting colorized output to your terminal screen.

configsvr: Specifies the target container name defined in your docker-compose.yml.

mongosh: The executable for the MongoDB Shell client installed inside the container.

--eval: Tells mongosh to execute the provided JavaScript string immediately and exit without opening an interactive terminal session.


